Binary releases built with the ROS 2 standalone option bundle the shared libraries below, and the
ROS 2 libraries they depend on (such as rcutils, rcpputils, rcl_yaml_param_parser, rcl_logging and
the message packages they use). They are copied from the ROS 2 distribution of the build (Humble or
Jazzy); the versions are those of that distribution.
- rcl, rclcpp, rmw, rmw_implementation, rmw_dds_common, rmw_fastrtps_cpp, rmw_cyclonedds_cpp
  (Apache-2.0), https://github.com/ros2
- rosidl runtime and typesupport libraries, rosidl_dynamic_typesupport_fastrtps (Jazzy)
  (Apache-2.0), https://github.com/ros2
- tracetools, rcl_logging_spdlog and rcl_interfaces (Jazzy) (Apache-2.0), https://github.com/ros2
- rcpputils (Apache-2.0 and BSD-3-Clause, as its package.xml declares), https://github.com/ros2/rcpputils
- LTTng-UST (liblttng-ust, liblttng-ust-common, liblttng-ust-tracepoint; LGPL-2.1, Copyright
  2009-2012 Mathieu Desnoyers and others), https://lttng.org, when the tracetools of the build links
  them (Jazzy on Ubuntu 24.04). The libraries are bundled unmodified as shared libraries; their
  source is that of the distribution package (Ubuntu `lttng-ust`, https://launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/lttng-ust)
  and of https://github.com/lttng/lttng-ust, and the LGPL-2.1 text is at
  https://www.gnu.org/licenses/old-licenses/lgpl-2.1.txt. They may be replaced by a compatible build.
- sensor_msgs, visualization_msgs and their message dependencies (Apache-2.0),
  https://github.com/ros2/common_interfaces
- radar_msgs (Apache-2.0), https://github.com/ros-perception/radar_msgs
- Fast DDS (Fast RTPS) and Fast CDR (Apache-2.0), https://github.com/eProsima/Fast-DDS,
  https://github.com/eProsima/Fast-CDR; foonathan/memory (Zlib), https://github.com/foonathan/memory
- Eclipse Cyclone DDS (EPL-2.0 OR BSD-3-Clause; distributed under BSD-3-Clause),
  https://github.com/eclipse-cyclonedds/cyclonedds
- Eclipse iceoryx (Linux) (Apache-2.0), https://github.com/eclipse-iceoryx/iceoryx
